/-
# Power subgroups of hyperbolic groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 11.74)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.74 (A. Yu. Olshanskii): let `G` be a
non-elementary hyperbolic group and `G^n` the subgroup generated by the `n`-th powers. (a) (M.
Gromov) Is `G / G^n` infinite for some `n = n(G)`? (b) Is `⋂_{n ≥ 1} G^n = 1`?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Index
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.VirtuallyCyclic
public import MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HyperbolicGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HyperbolicPowerSubgroupsKourovka11Problem74Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.74 (A. Yu.
Olshanskii). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700766 (`KOU-11.74`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Hyperbolic is MathlibExt's `Group.IsHyperbolic` (a finite generating set whose word metric is Gromov
hyperbolic). Non-elementary is "not virtually cyclic", Mathlib's `¬ Group.IsVirtuallyCyclic G` (no
cyclic subgroup of finite index), which excludes finite groups. `G / G^n` infinite is `G^n` of
infinite index (`G^n` is normal), which avoids forming the quotient.
-/

/-- `G^n`: the subgroup generated by the `n`-th powers of the elements of `G`. -/
def powerSubgroup (G : Type*) [Group G] (n : ℕ) : Subgroup G :=
  Subgroup.closure (Set.range fun g : G => g ^ n)

/-- Kourovka 11.74(a) (M. Gromov; A. Yu. Olshanskii): for every non-elementary hyperbolic group
`G` there is `n ≥ 1` such that `G / G^n` is infinite, i.e. `G^n` has infinite index. -/
def powerQuotientInfinite : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Group.IsHyperbolic G → ¬ Group.IsVirtuallyCyclic G →
    ∃ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ ¬ (powerSubgroup G n).FiniteIndex

/-- Kourovka 11.74(b) (A. Yu. Olshanskii): for every non-elementary hyperbolic group `G`,
`⋂_{n ≥ 1} G^n = 1`. -/
def powerSubgroupsTrivialIntersection : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], Group.IsHyperbolic G → ¬ Group.IsVirtuallyCyclic G →
    ∀ g : G, (∀ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n → g ∈ powerSubgroup G n) → g = 1

/--
Resolved true: Ivanov and Olshanskii prove that for every non-elementary hyperbolic group `G` the
quotient `G / G^n` is infinite for some `n`; the Kourovka Archive answers 11.74(a) "Yes, it is".
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.74 (A. Yu.
Olshanskii); resolution: S. V. Ivanov and A. Yu. Olshanskii, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 348, no. 6
(1996), 2091-2138, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.74: "a) Yes, it is; b) Yes, it is",
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted powerQuotientInfinite_holds : powerQuotientInfinite

/--
Resolved true: Ivanov and Olshanskii prove that `⋂_{n ≥ 1} G^n = 1` for every non-elementary
hyperbolic group `G`; the Kourovka Archive answers 11.74(b) "Yes, it is". Source: E. I. Khukhro and
V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 11.74 (A. Yu. Olshanskii);
resolution: S. V. Ivanov and A. Yu. Olshanskii, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 348, no. 6 (1996),
2091-2138, Kourovka Archive, Problem 11.74: "a) Yes, it is; b) Yes, it is",
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted powerSubgroupsTrivialIntersection_holds : powerSubgroupsTrivialIntersection

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.HyperbolicPowerSubgroupsKourovka11Problem74Wanted
